start     book
terminals word

# The D'ni's own books (design §4.2), and the only place a modifier is taught. Every book here should use
# one where the Age it makes shows what it did (§4.5): a `no` should leave out something the world would
# otherwise have. BookCheck fails any book that uses no grammatical word but `age`.

# Where a basic book is the ordinary world leaned one way, an advanced book is somewhere that could not be
# (Jonah, 2026-10-06): a scene, built from rarer words, that only a modifier makes sayable. Landforms mixed,
# monuments of copper and amethyst, a palette agreed between sun, sky, air, clouds, water and leaves, the
# phenomena taught nowhere else, the strange undergrounds, our own palm beaches. Fine ink is spent freely
# here; masterwork is not. A scene naming the pack's own worldgen (`palm_beach`, `torchflowers`) is judged on a
# server, which is no reason to leave it out.

# What these books must teach, because nothing else on the critical path does (plan, Phase 7 "Still open"):
# - Every grammatical word, each doing visible work: `and`, `only`, `no`, `in`, `everywhere`, `link`, `of`, and the four
#   rungs `scarce`, `few`, `plentiful` and `teeming`.
# - Danger: the words for a hostile crowd and the weather it suits, in common ink, scoring under the danger
#   line (`lines.pays_at`, art/danger.json) — no found Age earns a reward, so the hunt for deretheni starts
#   from what these teach rather than from the books themselves.
# - Half the scarab's habitat each: `torchflowers in jungle` in one book and `mud and sand pits in jungle` in
#   another, never both in one book, and never the warmth a colony also needs.
# Taught elsewhere, so not needed here: the city's words (the survey reports), `black sun` and `lava sea`
# (item frames), `polar` and `tidal` (the greenhouse's chest), `plasma` (beside the compounder).

# One lesson per kind of book, so a reader with two in hand can tell what each is showing them. The
# dangerous Ages are a quarter of the shelf: they are the road out of the early game.
book =
    [mingled_age]@2
    | [singled_age]@2
    | [spared_age]
    | [thronged_age]
    | [thinned_age]
    | [sited_age]
    | [widened_age]
    | [wonder_age]@2
    | [beset_age]@4
    | [flowered_jungle_age]
    | [pitted_jungle_age]
    | [linked_age]
    | [herded_age]

# `and`: two things laid together, so the world visibly holds both — two landforms in one country, two
# stones in one monument. A member says its own part of the world, so no aiming page follows one.
mingled_age =
    age [landform_pair] landmass [material_pair] [shape] [colour] sky [colour] clouds@3
    | age [landform_pair] landmass [material_pair] [shape] [night]@2
    | age archipelagic and pillared [semiprecious] arches [colour] waters [colour] sky
    | age canyoned and shattered red_sand surface sandfall orange sky
    | wondrous age skyborne and archipelagic [night]
    | age insular and archipelagic palm_beach [colour] waters white clouds
    | age patchy [hot_stone] and [dark_stone] landmass molten sea
    | age patchy [cold_stone] and [pale_stone] landmass inferno phenomena white sun

# `only`: one or two kinds of country and nothing else, dressed to suit.
singled_age =
    age only cherry_grove and meadow [sun_colour] sun [colour] air
    | age only ice_spikes blue_ice spikes [aurora_colour] aurora bright stars
    | age only pale_garden grey sky small moon
    | uncanny age only pale_garden green sky red sun
    | age only desert and badlands amethyst_block spikes sandfall orange sky
    | age only desert colossal sun orange sky
    | age only plains slime_block surface meteors phenomena [colour] sky

# `no`: something a world would have, left out where a visitor would miss it.
spared_age =
    age [land] no monsters bright stars colossal moon@2
    | age floating landmass no monsters [colour] sky [colour] clouds
    | age [land] no undead bright stars [aurora_colour] aurora
    | age [land] no undead and arthropods [sun_colour] sun
    | age verdant biomes no trees [colour] grass
    | age floating landmass no trees [colour] sky

# The upper rungs: monuments in numbers.
thronged_age =
    age [land] teeming [semiprecious] [shape] [colour] sky
    | age [land] plentiful glowstone rings bright stars

# The lower rungs: a few of something, set out in an emptier country.
thinned_age =
    age floating landmass few glowstone obelisks
    | age [land] few obsidian obelisks [colour] sky
    | age sheer scarce trees white sky

# `in`: a monument or a creature confined to one kind of country.
sited_age =
    age [land] amethyst_block spikes in desert yellow sky
    | age archipelagic prismarine pyramids in beach [colour] waters
    | age [land] glowstone rings in plains bright stars
    | age teeming parrot in jungle jungle
    | age plentiful axolotl in lush_caves

# `everywhere`: a creature in every kind of country, not only its own.
widened_age =
    age only swamp teeming frog everywhere green air
    | age deep water sea teeming axolotl everywhere
    | age insular reefs warm climate teeming axolotl everywhere [colour] waters
    | age teeming sniffer everywhere [colour] grass
    | age teeming allay everywhere [colour] leaves
    | age only flower_forest teeming bee everywhere honey_block [honey_shape]
    | age archipelagic palm_beach teeming parrot everywhere tropical climate

# `link in`: where a link into the Age arrives, somewhere it would not have — down in a cave, out on the water,
# beside a village. Rare on purpose (Jonah, 2026-10-21): one share of the shelf, and the only place it is taught.
linked_age =
    age [land] link in lush_caves bright stars
    | age archipelagic landmass link in sea [colour] waters
    | age [land] link in villages [colour] sky
    | age link in axolotl large chambered underground
    | age [warm_land] link in jungle tropical climate

# `of`: herds of something that never comes in them, and a shape made of a stone named after it. Each size
# said of the herds is how many come together, and one said of the creature how big each is.
herded_age =
    age [land] herds of parrot jungle biomes
    | age [land] teeming herds of colossal axolotl lush_caves biomes
    | age [land] colossal herds of fox [colour] leaves
    | age [land] minuscule herds of allay bright stars
    | age [land] pyramids of [semiprecious] [colour] sky

# The phenomena and the undergrounds taught nowhere else, each with a modifier to carry it.
wonder_age =
    age only badlands red_sand surface sandfall orange sky
    | age snow_block surface inferno phenomena only snowy_plains
    | age prismatic rainbow purple sky only cherry_grove
    | age [land] lattice underground glowstone and shroomlight veins
    | age [land] delved underground glowstone and shroomlight veins
    | age colossal chambered underground only lush_caves
    | age floating landmass hollow underground [colour] sky only plains
    | wondrous age skyborne bright stars [aurora_colour] aurora only plains

# Danger in common ink: a hostile crowd and a phenomenon that falls on whoever is out in it. Each pairs a
# creature with the weather it suits, at a thin crowd, so the Age stays under the danger threshold.
beset_age =
    age [land] few [monster] inferno phenomena lightless sky
    | age [land] few zombie and skeleton tempest phenomena
    | age [land] few zombie and skeleton blizzard phenomena
    | age [land] few husk scorching climate sandfall phenomena
    | age [land] few stray frozen climate blizzard phenomena
    | age [land] few spider deluge phenomena

# The scarab's habitat, half each, and never the warmth. Torchflowers are the pack's own, so this book is judged
# on a server.
flowered_jungle_age = age [warm_land] torchflowers in jungle jungle

pitted_jungle_age = age [warm_land] mud and sand pits in jungle tropical climate jungle

# Two landforms that make one strange country between them.
landform_pair =
    pillared and insular
    | sheer and cratered
    | skyborne and archipelagic
    | eroded and pillared
    | canyoned and shattered
    | pillared and gentle

# Two stones in one monument, each worth fine ink or set off by one that is.
material_pair =
    copper_block and amethyst_block
    | obsidian and crying_obsidian
    | prismarine and sea_lantern
    | quartz_block and calcite
    | glowstone and shroomlight

semiprecious = copper_block | amethyst_block | prismarine | quartz_block | obsidian | glowstone

shape = spikes | obelisks | arches | pyramids | rings

night = bright stars | [aurora_colour] aurora | small moon | colossal moon

land = [landform] landmass

landform = gentle | eroded | continental | archipelagic | insular | mountainous | riverine | canyoned | pillared

warm_land = [warm_landform] landmass

warm_landform = insular | archipelagic | gentle | riverine

hot_stone = netherrack | magma_block

dark_stone = blackstone | deepslate

cold_stone = snow_block | packed_ice

pale_stone = calcite | white_concrete

# Honey raised as a shape among the flowers, where a honey surface would have grown none.
honey_shape = spikes | piles | patches | rings | boulders | arches

colour = red | orange | yellow | green | cyan | blue | indigo | purple | magenta | white | black

sun_colour = red | white | yellow | cyan | indigo | magenta

aurora_colour = green | cyan | blue | indigo | purple | magenta | red | white

monster = zombie | skeleton | creeper | spider
